1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,460
To envision is to create an attractive picture for another person of the successful results you can achieve by working together.

2
00:00:07,140 --> 00:00:12,640
The picture should come alive for the other person. You can achieve this by using sensory detail.

3
00:00:12,880 --> 00:00:15,680
What will you see, hear, or experience?

4
00:00:15,960 --> 00:00:22,080
To be effective, the vision must demonstrate a potential outcome that the other person would see as positive and

5
00:00:22,340 --> 00:00:26,200
beneficial to him or her or to a group or cause that he or she values.

6
00:00:26,480 --> 00:00:30,060
The following are some examples of envisioning in action.

7
00:00:30,640 --> 00:00:36,160
I'm looking forward to seeing this product in the media as one of the top innovations of the year,

8
00:00:36,519 --> 00:00:39,220
along with a picture of the team that delivered it.

9
00:00:40,080 --> 00:00:44,640
Over the next five years, we're going to revolutionize the way we're perceived.

10
00:00:45,120 --> 00:00:50,920
Our customers will see us as a utility they use daily rather than as an occasional luxury.

11
00:00:51,600 --> 00:00:56,720
In six months, I believe we'll become the top performing sales team in the region.

12
00:00:56,880 --> 00:00:59,600
Others will look to us as the gold standard.

